          "prerequisites": [],
          "summary": "Impressionism broke from the academic tradition by prioritizing fleeting light, everyday subjects, and visible brushwork over polished historical and mythological scenes, arguing that direct perception was a valid basis for art. Post-Impressionism gathered four divergent responses to that legacy, ranging from structured form to expressive color and symbolic meaning, and the unit closes by translating these arguments into practical methods for reading a painting on a museum wall.",
